    "question": "A cubic equation with integer coefficients has roots $3$, $1 + \\sqrt{2}$ and $1 - \\sqrt{2}$.\nFind the equation in the form $x^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0$.",
    "marks": 10,
    "steps": [
     {
      "title": "Form the quadratic from the two surd roots",
      "lines": [
       {
        "tex": "(x - 1 - \\sqrt{2})(x - 1 + \\sqrt{2}) &= (x - 1)^2 - (\\sqrt{2})^2"
